   <property name="text">
    <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here is the lautering stage in which the wort is seperated from the solid grain particles. This process occurs in a lauter tun, where the wort is passed through a bed of spent grain. The grain acts as a filter, collecting any particulate and allowing the wort to pass through slits in the bottom of the bed as a clear liquid.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;After the main empyting process is complete, sparging begins. Sparging is the process of pouring water through the spent grain bed, to extract any sugars that may have been left behind.  &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
   </property>
